WEBVTT

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.375
We’ve entered the era of fast-evolving

00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:08.041
AI, which is pushing data centers
beyond their original purpose.

00:00:08.583 --> 00:00:11.875
Traditional infrastructure –
designed for general workloads

00:00:11.875 --> 00:00:16.500
– is now buckling under the weight
of massive model training, power-hungry

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:20.416
accelerators, and the relentless demand
for real-time data movement.

00:00:20.416 --> 00:00:25.958
To meet this challenge, OCP’s Open Systems
for AI initiative is reimagining IT

00:00:25.958 --> 00:00:31.500
infrastructure, starting from the silicon
to the server, the rack and beyond.

00:00:31.583 --> 00:00:35.416
The Open Systems for AI strategy enables
collaborative innovation

00:00:35.666 --> 00:00:39.500
without slowing down the rapid pace
of iteration in today’s AI systems.

00:00:39.791 --> 00:00:44.625
And OCP’s Open Cluster Designs
for AI initiative organizes reference

00:00:44.625 --> 00:00:48.625
architectures of these open systems
in AI pod and cluster designs.

00:00:49.083 --> 00:00:54.500
Compute trays carry the processing
load, housing GPUs, CPUs,

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.583
and AI accelerators,
all connected with ultra-fast links

00:00:58.583 --> 01:02.166
to eliminate bottlenecks
and improve data flow at the core.

01:02.500 --> 01:08.083
Inside the rack or pod, OCP’s Compute
and HBD switch trays

01:08.083 --> 01:10.791
form a High Bandwidth Domain;
an environment

01:10.791 --> 01:14.583
where AI accelerators can communicate
directly, instantly,

01:14.583 --> 01:16.833
and without interference
using technologies

01:16.833 --> 01:20.750
like NVLink, UALink or SUE.

01:20.750 --> 01:24.166
At scale, clusters of pods
connect through Infiniband

01:24.166 --> 01:29.583
or the open Ultra Ethernet standard,
a network built specifically for AI.

01:29.583 --> 01:32.625
It’s incredibly fast, highly flexible,

01:32.625 --> 01:35.875
and designed to route around congestion
before it even starts –

01:35.875 --> 01:40.291
much like how navigation apps
pre-emptively avoid traffic.

01:40.291 --> 01:42.333
This isn’t just an upgrade.

01:42.333 --> 01:45.708
It’s a complete rethink of the computer
and the server as its deployment

01:45.708 --> 01:50.125
unit, in order to be more modular,
scalable, and purpose-built

01:50.125 --> 01:54.375
to serve the next decade
of high-performance AI compute.